---
import ExampleSource from '../../components/ExampleSource.astro';
import Sample from '../../examples/editor/app';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { samplesSource } from '../../lib/links';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/site-path';
import documentSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/document.ts?raw';
import modelSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/model.ts?raw';
import messageSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/message.ts?raw';
import updateSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/update.ts?raw';
import sceneSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/scene.ts?raw';
import viewSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/view.ts?raw';
import commandSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/editor/command.ts?raw';
const sources = [{ name: 'document.ts', content: documentSource }, { name: 'model.ts', content: modelSource }, { name: 'message.ts', content: messageSource }, { name: 'update.ts', content: updateSource }, { name: 'scene.ts', content: sceneSource }, { name: 'view.ts', content: viewSource }, { name: 'command.ts', content: commandSource }];
---
<Layout title="Editor — effect-three">
  <section class="page-intro"><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/')}>← All examples</a><p class="eyebrow">EDITING</p><h1>A scene editor.</h1><p>Add things and lights, then select them by clicking, in the scene list, or by shift-dragging a box. Move, turn and scale them with the gizmo, and change anything else in the inspector, which is generated from the scene's own node schema and refuses what that schema refuses. Undo, redo, or jump to any step in the history; a change after an undo starts a branch, and the old one stays. Save the scene as a file, open it again, and see what changed since you saved. Frame a shot or light the scene by mood; an assistant can do the same through Foldkit DevTools. Open this page in a second tab and edit the same scene in both: every change goes through a lockstep session, so both tabs keep one document and one history.</p></section>
  <Sample client:load noMeta />
  <noscript><p>This example needs JavaScript and WebGL to render the scene.</p></noscript>
  <section class="closing-callout"><h2>The document is the Model.</h2><p>The scene being edited is a list of scene nodes in the Model. The gizmo, the selection box and the viewport gizmo are Foldkit submodels; the inspector is read from <code>SceneSchema.SceneNode</code>; the history is a tree of documents; a file is the schema's encoding; and the changes since saving are the kernel's own diff. Nothing here edits a three.js object directly.</p><a class="text-link" href={samplesSource + '/editor'}>Explore the example source →</a></section>
  <ExampleSource files={sources} />
</Layout>
